Example rules, in priority order (they show the syntax; they are not a good schedule for this system):
```
{"condition": "s = 0 & s2 = 1 & r2 = 2", "action": "u2_request_drive"}
{"condition": "gd & s = 2", "action": "u2_grant_drive"}
{"condition": "s1 = 0 & r1 = 0 & commUser != 0", "action": "u1_want_drive"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "u2_ready"}
```
Rule 1 lets user 2 ask for drive while the arbiter is idle. Rule 2 lets the arbiter grant a pending drive request of user 2. Rule 3 makes user 1 want drive while comm is held. The last rule is a catch-all default.
